NAME
    head - print the first lines

SYNOPSIS
    head [-N] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the first N lines (default 10) of the files named, read as
    one stream just as cat would print them (globs expand, "-" is the
    console), or of the console up to Ctrl-D. head is /BIN/HEAD.

OPTIONS
    -N    the first N lines (e.g. -5)

EXAMPLES
    head /FRUIT.TXT          the first 10 lines (all 7 of them)
    head -2 /FRUIT.TXT       apple 3 red, pear 5 green
    head -3 /MAN/C*          the first 3 lines of the lot

NOTES
    The count is over the whole stream, not per file.
    Removed from the P8X version: input from a pipe or a < redirect.
    New: several files, globs and "-".
    Ported from P8X os/commands/head.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
